<rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" version="2.0"><channel><title>User experience – justaddwater.dk</title><link>https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/tag/user-experience/</link><description>Instant Usability &amp;amp; Web Standards — static archive</description><language>en-US</language><atom:link href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/tag/user-experience/feed/" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml" /><item><title>Sell More: Add Next Steps To Your Status Messages</title><link>https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/2009/09/21/sell-more-add-next-steps-to-your-status-messages/</link><guid isPermaLink="false">http://justaddwater.dk/?p=1146</guid><dc:creator>Jesper Rønn-Jensen</dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2009 21:02:12 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;Sometimes, when doing web development, we forget that not everybody are as familiar with the web jargon as ourselves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This example from Pixum (internet photo developer) shows a good detail:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="pixum-status-message-with-shopping-cart-affordance-crop" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1149" height="210" sizes="(max-width: 443px) 100vw, 443px" src="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2009/09/pixum-status-message-with-shopping-cart-affordance-crop1.png" srcset="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2009/09/pixum-status-message-with-shopping-cart-affordance-crop1.png 443w, https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2009/09/pixum-status-message-with-shopping-cart-affordance-crop1-300x142.png 300w" title="pixum-status-message-with-shopping-cart-affordance-crop" width="443"/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;The status message from Pixum gives immediate feedback that makes it easy to go to next step&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Note that the status message contains a link to the shopping basket to provide easy way to purchase. This design decision will probably decrease number of abandoned shopping carts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Important lessons:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide help where users need it&lt;/strong&gt; — not hidden in help windows where people only go when they give up using your app.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Make sure that &lt;strong&gt;the most important action is the most visible on page at the current time&lt;/strong&gt;. No need to visually hint the shopping basket until there is something in it.&lt;/p&gt;
</description></item><item><title>Bad Usability Calendar 2009 Is Out</title><link>https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/2009/01/15/bad-usability-calendar-2009-is-out/</link><guid isPermaLink="false">http://justaddwater.dk/?p=1007</guid><dc:creator>Jesper Rønn-Jensen</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 15 Jan 2009 11:12:40 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;My Norwegian friend Eidar from NetLife Research pointed out that the 2009 version of the bad usability calendar is now online. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learning by bad examples is often a good way in discussing usability with people that are not hardcore usability people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="" class="alignnone" data-original-url="http://www.badusability.com/img/international/bad-usability-calendar-2009-thumbnail.png" height="315" src="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/archive-assets/external/272efddf55e1a1f8e24d88ef.png" width="237"/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I’m currently wrapping a couple of A3 calendars in plastic to use as posters here at the office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Download from: &lt;a href="http://www.badusability.com/"&gt;Badusability.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Previous articles:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/2008/01/17/bad-usability-calendar-2008/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Bad Usability Calendar 2008"&gt;Bad Usability Calendar 2008&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/2007/01/27/bad-usability-calendar-2007-finally-ready/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Bad Usability Calendar 2007 Finally Ready"&gt;Bad Usability Calendar 2007 Finally Ready&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/2006/10/16/bad-usability-calendar/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Bad Usability Calendar"&gt;Bad Usability Calendar&lt;/a&gt; (2005 and 2006)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description></item><item><title>Bad Usability Calendar 2008</title><link>https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/2008/01/17/bad-usability-calendar-2008/</link><guid isPermaLink="false">http://justaddwater.dk/2008/01/17/bad-usability-calendar-2008/</guid><dc:creator>Jesper Rønn-Jensen</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 17 Jan 2008 18:19:29 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;My Norwegian friend Eidar just wrote to inform me that their company (&lt;a href="http://www.netliferesearch.no/"&gt;Netlife Research&lt;/a&gt;) has finally released Bad Usability Calendar 2008. Last year, the calendar got quite popular and even Jakob Nielsen mentioned it in &lt;a href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/2007/02/12/jakob-nielsen-mentions-bad-usability-calendar-in-latest-newsletter/"&gt;one of his newsletters.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This year, I’m more than ever looking forward to use it. The calendar has — as always — 12 brilliant examples of how not to build a calendar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="bad-usability-calendar-2008-september.png" src="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2008/01/bad-usability-calendar-2008-september.png"/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What’s even better, the calendar now has it’s own dedicated website: &lt;a href="http://www.badusability.com"&gt;www.badusability.com&lt;/a&gt;, where it’s also possible to upload photos of the calendar in the wild.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Like last year, I’ll ask &lt;a href="http://baekdal.com"&gt;Thomas Baekdal&lt;/a&gt; to work with me on a Danish version… unless somebody else puts it up before us (if you plan to translate it, drop me a note so I don’t waste the time).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Download from &lt;a href="http://www.badusability.com"&gt;www.badusability.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mention last year: &lt;a href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/2007/02/09/bad-usability-calendar-2007-in-danish/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Bad Usability Calendar 2007 in Danish"&gt;Bad Usability Calendar 2007 in Danish&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;small&gt;Technorati Tags: &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/usability" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/usability/" rel="tag"&gt;usability&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/calendar" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/calendar/" rel="tag"&gt; calendar&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/humour" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/humour/" rel="tag"&gt; humour&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description></item><item><title>Bad Usability Calendar 2008 Open For Proposals</title><link>https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/2007/11/28/bad-usability-calendar-2008-open-for-proposals/</link><guid isPermaLink="false">http://justaddwater.dk/2007/11/28/bad-usability-calendar-2008-open-for-proposals/</guid><dc:creator>Jesper Rønn-Jensen</dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 28 Nov 2007 20:04:11 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;Just a quick note to mention that my friend Eidar and his colleagues at Netlife Research in Norway are now preparing the 2008 version of the Bad Usability Calendar. Please do post your proposals as a bad usability calendar is a perfect wallpaper and I have used it on several occasions for raising awareness about usability in project teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2006/10/screenshot-bad-usability-calendar1.png" title="Bad usability calendar 2006 screenshot"&gt;&lt;img alt="Bad usability calendar 2006 screenshot" src="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2006/10/screenshot-bad-usability-calendar1.png"/&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From this year’s official announcement you can see that this time there are prizes for the best suggestions:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote cite="http://www.iallenkelhet.no/bad-usability-calendar-2008-under-construction-give-us-your-ideas"&gt;&lt;p&gt;The best idea will get an honorable mention, as well as a numbered limited edition of the 2008 Bad Usability Calendar. All suggestions that make the final cut will get awarded.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More info:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Netlife Research: &lt;a href="http://www.iallenkelhet.no/bad-usability-calendar-2008-under-construction-give-us-your-ideas"&gt;Bad Usability Calendar 2008 under construction&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Justaddwater.dk: &lt;a href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/2007/02/09/bad-usability-calendar-2007-in-danish/" title="Justaddwater.dk: Bad Usability Calendar 2007 in Danish"&gt;Bad Usability Calendar 2007 in Danish&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Justaddwater.dk: &lt;a href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/2007/01/27/bad-usability-calendar-2007-finally-ready/" rel="bookmark" title="Justaddwater.dk: Bad Usability Calendar 2007 Finally Ready"&gt;Bad Usability Calendar 2007 Finally Ready&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Justaddwater.dk: &lt;a href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/2006/10/16/bad-usability-calendar/" rel="bookmark" title="Justaddwater.dk: Bad Usability Calendar 2006"&gt;Bad Usability Calendar (2006)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;small&gt;Technorati Tags: &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/usability" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/usability/" rel="tag"&gt;usability&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/bad+usability+calendar" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/bad-usability-calendar/" rel="tag"&gt; bad usability calendar&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/calendar" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/calendar/" rel="tag"&gt; calendar&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/2008" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/2008/" rel="tag"&gt; 2008&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description></item><item><title>Bad Usability Calendar 2007 in Danish</title><link>https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/2007/02/09/bad-usability-calendar-2007-in-danish/</link><guid isPermaLink="false">http://justaddwater.dk/2007/02/09/bad-usability-calendar-2007-in-danish/</guid><dc:creator>Jesper Rønn-Jensen</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 09 Feb 2007 09:48:43 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;Thomas Baekdal and I have translated and are now publishing Bad Usability Calendar 2007 in Danish.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I can highly recommend using this calendar in projects as wallpaper. But good luck on using it for actual planning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Screenshot of Danish Bad Usability Calendar (dårlig brugervenlighed kalender 2007)" id="image544" src="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2007/02/bad-usability-calendar-2007-danish-dk-screenshot.jpg"/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This year’s version contains advice regarding AJAX, overwhelming use of graphics, advertising, and much more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Download Bad Usability Calendar 2007&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="http://iallenkelhet.no/nedlast/bad_usability_calendar_07_english_A3.pdf"&gt;English&lt;/a&gt; &lt;small&gt;(560KB PDF)&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.iallenkelhet.no/nedlast/bad_usability_calendar_07_norsk_A3.pdf"&gt;Norwegian&lt;/a&gt; &lt;small&gt;(1.2 MB PDF)&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2007/02/bad_usability_calendar_07-da-opt.pdf" id="p543" title="Download Bad Usability Calendar (Danish version)"&gt;Danish&lt;/a&gt; &lt;small&gt;(3.3 MB PDF)&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Related articles:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thomas Baekdal: &lt;a href="http://www.baekdal.com/notes/work/bad-usability-2007/"&gt;Bad Usability Calendar – in Danish&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Netlife Research: &lt;a href="http://www.iallenkelhet.no/bad-usability-calendar-2007-is-here"&gt;Bad Usability Calendar 2007 is here!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Justadddwater.dk: &lt;a href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/2007/01/27/bad-usability-calendar-2007-finally-ready/" rel="bookmark" title="Justaddwater.dk: Bad Usability Calendar 2007 Finally Ready"&gt;Bad Usability Calendar 2007 Finally Ready&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Justaddwater.dk: &lt;a href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/2006/10/16/bad-usability-calendar/" rel="bookmark" title="Justaddwater.dk: Bad Usability Calendar 2006"&gt;Bad Usability Calendar (2006)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;small&gt;Technorati Tags: &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/usability" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/usability/" rel="tag"&gt; usability&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/accessibility" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/accessibility/" rel="tag"&gt;  accessibility&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/calendar" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/calendar/" rel="tag"&gt;  calendar&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/anti-usability" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/anti-usability/" rel="tag"&gt;  anti-usability&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/user+experience" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/user-experience/" rel="tag"&gt;  user experience&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/ux" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/ux/" rel="tag"&gt;  ux&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/uxp" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/uxp/" rel="tag"&gt;  uxp&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/humor" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/humor/" rel="tag"&gt;  humor&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/ajax" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/ajax/" rel="tag"&gt; ajax&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description></item><item><title>Bad Usability Calendar 2007 Finally Ready</title><link>https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/2007/01/27/bad-usability-calendar-2007-finally-ready/</link><guid isPermaLink="false">http://justaddwater.dk/2007/01/27/bad-usability-calendar-2007-finally-ready/</guid><dc:creator>Jesper Rønn-Jensen</dc:creator><pubDate>Sat, 27 Jan 2007 08:57:31 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;I’ve been waiting for this with excitement: Eidar and the rest of NetLife Research in Norway have finally &lt;a href="http://www.iallenkelhet.no/bad-usability-calendar-2007-is-here"&gt;released the 2007 version of Bad Usability Calendar&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Direct download: &lt;a href="http://iallenkelhet.no/nedlast/bad_usability_calendar_07_english_A3.pdf"&gt;Bad Usability Calendar 2007&lt;/a&gt; (1.2 MB PDF)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Very nice to see that the calendar actually is released under a Creative Commons license, so you can translate it into you native language as long as you keep the reference to NetLife Research.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Related posts:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/2006/10/16/bad-usability-calendar/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link: Bad Usability Calendar"&gt;Bad Usability Calendar&lt;/a&gt; (2006)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/2006/11/10/bad-usability-calendar-2007-open-for-proposals/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link: Bad Usability Calendar 2007 open for proposals"&gt;Bad Usability Calendar 2007 open for proposals&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;small&gt;Technorati Tags: &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/usability" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/usability/" rel="tag"&gt; usability&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/accessibility" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/accessibility/" rel="tag"&gt;  accessibility&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/calendar" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/calendar/" rel="tag"&gt;  calendar&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/anti-usability" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/anti-usability/" rel="tag"&gt;  anti-usability&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/user+experience" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/user-experience/" rel="tag"&gt;  user experience&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/ux" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/ux/" rel="tag"&gt;  ux&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/uxp" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/uxp/" rel="tag"&gt;  uxp&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/humor" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/humor/" rel="tag"&gt;  humor&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description></item><item><title>Bad Usability Calendar 2007 open for proposals</title><link>https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/2006/11/10/bad-usability-calendar-2007-open-for-proposals/</link><guid isPermaLink="false">http://justaddwater.dk/2006/11/10/bad-usability-calendar-2007-open-for-proposals/</guid><dc:creator>Jesper Rønn-Jensen</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 10 Nov 2006 08:37:38 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;Our Norwegian friends at Netlife Research have opened for suggestions to next years Bad Usability Calendar. I already used the &lt;a href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/2006/10/16/bad-usability-calendar/" title="Justaddwater.dk: Bad Usability Calendar 2006"&gt;2006 calendar with great impact&lt;/a&gt; in my professional engagements, and I’m really looking forward to next year’s version.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote cite="http://www.iallenkelhet.no/the-worst-12-usability-problems-give-us-your-ideas-for-bad-usability-calendar-2007"&gt;&lt;p&gt;To make a calendar for 2007 that has the same level of unusual unusefulness, we would like your feedback.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Give us your best examples of bad usability!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The best idea will get an honourable mention, as well as a numbered limited edition of the 2007 Bad Usability Calendar. All suggestions that make the final cut will get a prize.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need inspiration, check out the Bad Usability Calendars for &lt;a data-original-url="http://www.netliferesearch.com/files/kalender_netlife_V3_mai2005.jpg" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/archive-assets/external/f2c8bf09804044a4b7d5480c.jpg"&gt;2005&lt;/a&gt;(jpg), and &lt;a href="http://www.netliferesearch.com/files/kalender_2006_eng_A3.pdf"&gt;2006&lt;/a&gt; (pdf). Thank you in advance for all your help. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Add your suggestions at their blog IAllEnkelhet.no (which means something like “in all it’s simplicity”).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For inspiration, I really enjoy the suggestion from Christian Watson (&lt;a href="http://www.smileycat.com/"&gt;smileycat&lt;/a&gt;):&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;img alt="Bad usability calendar example: Flash intro hides content" data-original-url="http://www.smileycat.com/miaow/archives/images/misc/smileycat-bad-usability.gif" src="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/archive-assets/external/6ffacd7eb5205897dac980a7.gif"/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Read more at Netlife Research: &lt;a href="http://www.iallenkelhet.no/the-worst-12-usability-problems-give-us-your-ideas-for-bad-usability-calendar-2007" title="IAllEnkelhet.no:  The worst 12 usability problems - give us your ideas for Bad Usability Calendar 2007"&gt;Suggestions for 2007 calendar&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;small&gt;Technorati Tags: &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/usability" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/usability/" rel="tag"&gt;usability&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/accessibility" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/accessibility/" rel="tag"&gt;  accessibility&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/calendar" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/calendar/" rel="tag"&gt;  calendar&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/anti-usability" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/anti-usability/" rel="tag"&gt;  anti-usability&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/user+experience" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/user-experience/" rel="tag"&gt;  user experience&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/ux" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/ux/" rel="tag"&gt;  ux&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/uxp" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/uxp/" rel="tag"&gt;  uxp&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a data-original-url="http://technorati.com/tag/humor" href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/topics/humor/" rel="tag"&gt; humor&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description></item></channel></rss>